arresting you on suspicion of the murder  of your late wife  joking  this dash cam footage from a police car  shows ian stewart's indignant reaction  when officers arrested him for the 2010  murder of his wife diane at the home  they shared in cambridgeshire  the jury was told on the opening day of  this trial that 61 year old stewart was  already a convicted murderer he'd killed  his fiancee the children's author helen  bailey in 2016 in hertfordshire and  hidden her body in a cesspit while she  was planning their wedding he was  planning her murder he stood to gain 1.8  million pounds plus two properties  it was that conviction that prompted  detectives to look at the sudden death  six years earlier of 47 year old diane  her death had initially been put down to  an epileptic fit  this was the 999 call stewart made after  he'd murdered her the judge described it  as a charade is she awake no no she's  not awake is she breathing  is she breathing no i don't think so in  a statement diane's sister wendy and  brother christopher said diane was a  very special caring and capable person  she will always be greatly loved and  hugely missed by her family and all who  knew her  she's not awake you didn't think that  she was breathing how did you check if  you were breathing  during police interviews stewart said  nothing  i believe that he felt he was  more intelligent and more superior to  the officers that were investigating him  i think he really looked down on the  investigation and what we were trying to  achieve  he received 96 000 pounds in insurance  payouts and cash after diane's death the  judge described him as a callous man who  had carried out strikingly similar  murders  the whole life order means ian stewart  will die behind bars  ender brady sky news in cambridgeshire
 

